cooking in Zelda breath of the wild is  essential to your survival but there are  quite a few food-related things that the  game doesn't really explain if you're  not sure where to start or what you even  need to cook we've got you covered we  also have more tips including nine  things the game doesn't tell you first  you need to gather some ingredients  there are four main types regular food  food with a bonus effect critters and  insects and monster parts you can climb  trees to get apples pick spicy peppers  off the vine catch Restless crickets in  the grass and kill becau blends to get  their horns just to name a few most  ingredients will have their uses laid  out in their description so if you're  absolutely lost start there there are  generally three types of dishes you can  make basic ones that only fill your  hearts elixirs that just give you a buff  in status dishes that both fill your  hearts and give you a buff combine basic  food items for heart dishes mix monster  parts and critters for elixirs and throw  in a status effect food like spicy  peppers with normal food to get status  dishes  be warned food only goes with other food  and critters go with monster parts  combining them in creative ways will get  you dubious food which will technically  fill some of your hearts but you could  use those ingredients for something  better next find a cooking pot they can  be in town stables and Picabo and camps  and you need to light a flame underneath  them to start cooking they're often near  an open flame so just use a torch to  light it side note you can also start an  emergency fire of your own by dropping  wood and flint and hitting it with a  sword if you can't find a cooking pot  you can drop most food near the fire to  quickly roast it and slightly increase  how many hearts it'll fill it will  literally catch fire but if you keep an  eye on it and pick it up as soon as it's  fully cooked it won't burn to a crisp  Plus roasted items stack in your  inventory unlike cook dishes to use a  cooking pot go into your inventory  select the ingredient you want to use  and choose hold you can hold up to five  ingredients at a time once you have your  ingredients ready stand over the pot and  choose cook to cook  you'll want plenty of health dishes on  hand before you go anywhere you can  combine things like meat fish fruits  veggies mushrooms and a variety of  plants in a pot for something tasty and  nutritious but don't go crazy adding  ingredients if you only have a few  hearts stick to one or two ingredients  if you're at the very beginning and if  you have more hearts to fill at a high  role herb or a few Hylian shrooms to  some raw meat for an easy but more  filling dish for tons of hearts cook  with a hearty ingredient like a hardy  truffle the dish you make will grant you  full recovery and extra hearts for a  time and if you throw in a ferry you'll  get a lot more hearts from whatever you  make together don't worry it won't  actually cook the ferry adding food with  special effects to a basic dish will  make it the Status version of that dish  so you can make a mushroom skewer by  cooking a Hylian shroom and you can make  an energizing mushroom skewer by adding  a stamina filling stem mellow shroom to  that basic dish add more of the effect  ingredient to increase the potency of  the buff and add more of the basic food  to increase the hearts you'll get from  it just don't mix two or more kinds of  effects because they'll just cancel each  other out elixirs are a bit more  complicated there are two factors to  look for the quality of the puff and the  time it lasts buffs can be low mid or  high level and generally correspond to  the kind of critter you use and the buff  timer can usually be extended by adding  more monster parts note that critters  include small animals like frogs as well  as insects but not snails for some  reason sometimes you'll get an extra  special sound effect when cooking and  that means you had a critical success  you'll get a bonus like more hearts or a  better buff at random if you cook during  a Blood Moon you're guaranteed a  critical success so time you're cooking  accordingly finally make sure you have a  good balance of heart dishes status  dishes and elixirs ready for your  adventures since buffs don't stack  eating an elaborate status dish when you  only need to fill your hearts would wipe  whatever status you already have and if  you don't need the buff at all then it's  a total waste of course like most of  breadth of the wild cooking is a lot of  trial and error let us know in the  comments what your favorite recipes are  and subscribe so you don't miss any more  Zelda tips  [Music]  you
 

